{
  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a systematic upward bias during high-volatility periods characterized by recent price spikes (e.g., >85 EUR) and low sentiment scores.",
    "Forecasts fail to capture immediate mean reversion after sharp rallies, instead projecting continued linear growth that ignores volatility clustering.",
    "When sentiment is near zero or slightly positive (0.00-0.20) following a price surge, the model significantly overestimates the 30-day trajectory by 5-10 EUR compared to true outcomes.",
    "The model lacks sensitivity to 'noise' in short-term history; it smooths out erratic daily movements into a false trend line that diverges sharply from actual path-dependent volatility.",
    "Correction heuristic: Apply a negative adjustment factor of approximately -6% to the forecasted 30-day target when the last 5 days show >10 EUR range expansion and sentiment remains neutral."
  ]
}
